      <abstract>
       <para>Ansible Core is an agentless IT automation engine in &productname; that simplifies configuration management, application deployment and task orchestration. By defining infrastructure as code using declarative playbooks, administrators can efficiently automate and scale system administration across managed nodes over SSH without requiring client-side agent software.</para>
  <para><emphasis>Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
  <itemizedlist>
    <listitem>
      <para>Linux fundamentals, including basic commands, file permissions and CLI usage</para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
      <para>Networking basics, including IP addresses, SSH authentication, hostnames and ports</para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
      <para>Basic understanding of YAML syntax and document structure</para>
    </listitem>
  </itemizedlist>
